Article 20
(1) The fulfillment of basic health and welfare as referred to in Article 14 letter c, includes:
a. provision of health facilities and infrastructure for Children;
b. provision of human resources in the health sector;
c. guidance on the Protection and maintenance of Children's health, covering:
1. guidance on child growth health in efforts to reduce infant mortality rates and malnutrition rates for children;
2. guidance on providing early breastfeeding initiation, exclusive breast milk and continuous breast milk directly;
3. guidance on providing complete immunization for children; and
4. guidance on providing healthy, balanced, and safe food for Children;
d. provision of welfare facilities and infrastructure for Children, covering:
1. guidance on child-friendly households;
2. provision of child-friendly public spaces;
3. guidance on the availability of child-friendly infrastructure in public spaces;
4. guidance on organizing Children's playgrounds;
5. guidance on Child care facilities;
6. guidance on the availability of breastfeeding (lactation) rooms;
7. guidance on the availability of child-friendly places of worship;
8. provision and guidance on the availability of green open spaces;
9. guidance on organizing smoke-free areas; and
10. guidance on organizing child-friendly public transportation;
e. provision of accessibility facilities and infrastructure for Children with disabilities;
f. maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation of neglected children;
g. guidance on improving the welfare of poor families.
(2) Guidance on child-friendly households as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d number 1, is carried out in efforts to fulfill access to clean water and proper sanitation.
